  "readmeFile": "ReadMe.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### 7.0.286\nFix: AddRemoteTls route unmarshal no longer writes out of bounds when the password field length exceeds the decoded password (heap corruption). The cleartext password is now decoded into owned buffers and scrubbed safely.\nFix: AddRemoteTls route unmarshal now advances the read offset past the password field, so the key and host fields are parsed from the correct position.\nFix: UDP discovery no longer over-reads adjacent heap memory when a discovery reply contains a too-short TargetOs or TcVersion tag (out-of-bounds read / information disclosure). The tag length is now validated before the fixed-size structure is read.\nFix: UDP discovery now rejects packets whose declared tag count is negative, exceeds 256, or exceeds what the remaining bytes can contain, before allocating the tag array. This prevents a crafted 28-byte packet from forcing a multi-gigabyte allocation (OutOfMemoryException / denial of service). The discovery listener now also skips malformed packets instead of terminating.\nFix: AddRoute request marshaller now rejects cbAddNetIds values exceeding 64 or exceeding what the remaining request bytes can hold, before allocating the AdsSysAddNetId array. This prevents a single AddRoute request from forcing a multi-gigabyte allocation and crashing the system service.\nFix: StringMarshaler LengthPrefix mode now validates the wire length against remaining source bytes before calling GetString, preventing an uncaught exception from overflow or out-of-range values.\n### 7.0.280\nFix: Issue starting communication with 32-Bit TwinCAT (hanging on TcpLoopback)\n### 7.0.263\nBreaking Change: Removing TwinCAT.Ads.AdsErrorCode.Succeeded (use TwincAT.AdsErrorCode.NoError instead). The removed value was already obsolelete and created some quirks in specific circumstances.\n### 7.0.165\nChange: TwinCAT.TypeSystem.IEnumValue.Primitive renamed to IEnumValue.Value to represent the Primitive value of the enum member (old property remains marked as obsolete).\nChange: TwinCAT.TypeSystem.IEnumValue.ManagedBaseType renamed to IEnumValue.BaseType to represent the managed base type of the enum member (old property remains marked as obsolete).\n### 7.0.133\nEnh: New extension methods TwinCAT.Ads.AdsClientExtensions.RepeatedWriteAsync / TwinCAT.Ads.AdsClientExtensions.RepeatedWrite \n### 7.0.109\nEnh: Overall optimizations for performance gains and less memory pressure. More internal usage of ReadOnlyMemory<byte> instead of byte[] reduces the amount of array copy operations.\n### 7.0.36\nBreaking Change: Removes .NET6 as Dependency (out-of-support)\n### 7.0\nEnh: Supports **locally** installed TwinCAT 2 (via PInvoke channel)\nEnh: Supports internal communication via UnixSockets, TCP/IP Loopback and PInvoke\nEnh: TargetFramework dependencies changed to net8.0, net6.0, netstandard2.0",
